      "description": "Watch Southampton vs West Ham highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. On a night filled with cup drama at St Mary's Stadium, Southampton and West Ham United clashed on August 25, 2026, with both sides eager to secure their progress in the Carabao Cup . The match promised a high-octane battle as both managers looked to balance rotation with the competitive edge needed for knockout football. Early Breakthrough for the Saints Southampton enjoyed the perfect start, taking the lead just 10 minutes into the contest. Léo Scienza found space in the centre of the box and clinicaly placed a right-footed shot into the bottom left corner to ignite the home crowd. The lead energized the hosts, but West Ham soon found their footing. Joël Piroe was a constant threat, forcing two sharp saves from Daniel Peretz as the Hammers searched for a way back. Their persistence eventually paid off in the 41st minute when Lewis Orford delivered a pinpoint cross from a corner, allowing Joshua Ajala to power a header into the high centre of the goal to level the score before halftime. Ajala Turns the Tide The second half saw the momentum shift firmly in favor of the visitors. In the 53rd minute, Joshua Ajala struck again, finding the net with a composed right-footed finish from the centre of the box to give the Hammers their first lead of the night. Southampton attempted to regain control with a flurry of tactical substitutions, introducing Flynn Downes , Samuel Edozie , and Kuryu Matsuki to inject fresh energy into their midfield and attack. However, the visitors remained disciplined and continued to absorb pressure while looking dangerous on the break. Clinical Finish from the Hammers As the clock ticked down, the quality of West Ham’s substitutes proved decisive. Valentín Castellanos , who had come off the bench, extended the lead in the 75th minute with a close-range finish following an assist from Joël Veltman . The Saints pushed forward in a desperate attempt to stay in the competition, with Finn Azaz seeing his long-range effort saved. However, Jarrod Bowen put the result beyond doubt in the 84th minute, slotting home a left-footed shot after a clever pass from Lewis Orford . Despite a late save by Daniel Peretz to deny Manor Solomon , the match ended 1-4, confirming a dominant away victory for the London side."
